  · BEHAVIORAL DRIFT (HARD — how the protagonist physically inhabits this scene; the AXIS expressed through ACTION, not internal narration):
      – She INTERRUPTS more. Cuts other characters off mid-sentence to redirect to the task. The interruption is small (a single word, a question reframed) — never aggressive, just impatient with non-task content.
